---
title: App Setup
---

Prepare NAHPU before fieldwork so the app reflects your team's protocols and every device is ready to record data offline.

## Configure the app

- Customize dropdown values for specimen fields, collection methods, preparation types, and personnel.
- Create useful presets for repeated cataloging workflows and review them with the whole team.
- Install NAHPU from the [Installation guide](../installation), then update it before departure while you still have reliable internet access.
- Open the app after updating and confirm that projects, settings, and permissions are available.

## Prepare a project

Create a project with a short, descriptive name, assign the team members, and define the target taxa and catalog format. Confirm the project dates and site-identifier convention before collecting begins. The [Projects guide](../usages/projects) describes project creation and dashboard operations in detail.

## Run a mock catalog session

Use a real or representative specimen to rehearse the complete workflow: create a record, enter required values, generate a site coordinate when appropriate, attach media, save the record, and review it from the project dashboard. Repeat the exercise on every field device and resolve differences before departure.

## Confirm field readiness

Before leaving, confirm that each device has enough storage, a charged battery and backup power, the latest NAHPU version, the correct project, and the required location and camera permissions. Test airplane-mode operation if the field site may lack connectivity, and make one test backup that can be restored.
